vidyut-lipi 0.2.0: build the Unicode normalization tables once.

In WASM builds, to_nfc() and to_nfd() rebuilt their lookup tables from every
scheme on each call. transliterate() normalizes its input first, so each call
paid about 22 us before doing any work, and word-by-word use was ~15x slower
than whole-text use. The tables are pure functions of the static scheme data,
so they are now built on first use and kept in a OnceLock. Output is unchanged.

Upstream: https://github.com/ambuda-org/vidyut (vidyut-lipi/src/unicode_norm.rs,
still rebuilding per call on main as of 2026-11-05).

